WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
2009. The US economy is deep in recession.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.510
Congress passes the American
Recovery and Reinvestment Act.

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.360
It mixes government spending,
tax cuts and transfers.

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.850
Estimated cost when passed:
about 787 billion dollars.

5
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.720
So when a slump hits,

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.260
can a government spend its way out of it?

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.030
In this mission, you'll
calculate how big a spending

8
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.920
increase or tax cut a gap needs.

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.870
Then you'll use a graph lab:

10
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.850
raise government spending
and watch real GDP respond.

11
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.870
Your mission: figure out what
fiscal policy can do in a recession,

12
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.390
and what can hold it back.
